  "summary": "404 Media obtained a July bulletin from the Orange County Intelligence Assessment Center, a fusion center, warning California police that city council meetings about Flock surveillance cameras could be targets for 'extremists' and listing protected First Amendment activities (large turnout, emotional confrontations, media presence) as potential public safety risks. The bulletin acknowledged no credible threats and cited LAPD's recent termination of its Flock contract as potentially emboldening anti-surveillance organizers.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "City-hosted events (i.e., city council meetings) may be viewed by extremists as a desirable target. Partners are encouraged to review for signs of suspicious activity",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    },
    {
      "quote": "providing organizers and participants with a high-profile local example that could increase turnout and place additional public pressure on City Council members",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "no specific and credible threats found",
      "paragraph_idx": 5
    }
